Here is the extended C# code that maintains the existing functionality while adding the option to export the report in CSV format:

```csharp
using System;
using System.IO;

public class SummaryReport
{
    public string Title { get; set; }
    public string Content { get; set; }

    public override string ToString()
    {
        return $"Title: {Title}\nContent: {Content}";
    }
}

public class ReportGenerator
{
    public void GenerateReport(SummaryReport report, bool exportToCsv = false, string filePath = null)
    {
        // Existing functionality: Output summary report to console
        Console.WriteLine("Report Summary:");
        Console.WriteLine(report.ToString());

        // New functionality: Export to CSV if requested
        if (exportToCsv)
        {
            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(filePath))
            {
                filePath = "report.csv";
            }

            try
            {
                using (var writer = new StreamWriter(filePath))
                {
                    // Write CSV header
                    writer.WriteLine("Title,Content");

                    // Write report data
                    // Note: If Content contains commas or newlines, it should be quoted
                    string escapedContent = report.Content.Replace("\"", "\"\"");
                    writer.WriteLine($"\"{report.Title}\",\"{escapedContent}\"");
                }

                Console.WriteLine($"Report exported to CSV: {filePath}");
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                Console.WriteLine($"Error exporting report to CSV: {ex.Message}");
            }
        }
    }
}
```

### Explanation of Changes:
1. **Method Signature Update**: Added optional parameters `exportToCsv` (default `false`) and `filePath` (default `null`) to allow users to opt into CSV export without breaking existing calls.
2. **CSV Export Logic**:
   - If `exportToCsv` is `true`, the method creates a CSV file.
   - It writes a header row (`Title,Content`).
   - It writes the report's `Title` and `Content` as a CSV row, properly escaping double quotes within the content to ensure valid CSV formatting.
